      "category": "QueuedThreadPool",
      "signature": "CreateForkable(Target, In Num Queued Threads, Stack Size, Thread Priority, Name)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FQueuedThreadPool*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Num Queued Threads",
          "type": "UInt"
        },
        {
          "name": "Stack Size",
          "type": "UInt",
          "default": "(32 * 1024)"
        },
        {
          "name": "Thread Priority",
          "type": "EThreadPriority",
          "default": "TPri_Normal"
        },
        {
          "name": "Name",
          "type": "TCHAR*",
          "default": "TEXT(\"UnknownThreadPool\")"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Bool",
      "docs": "Creates the thread pool with the specified number of forkable threads (see FForkProcessHelper)\nCurrently only works after the process has been forked because GetSingleThreadInterface() isn't implemented for pooled threads\n@param InNumQueuedThreads Specifies the number of threads to use in the pool\n@param StackSize The size of stack the threads in the pool need (32K default)\n@param ThreadPriority priority of new pool thread\n@param Name optional name for the pool to be used for instrumentation\n@return Whether the pool creation was successful or not"
    },
